.Dd March 25, 2019
.Dt IPKG 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ipkg
.Nd zone brand for running a full copy of OpenIndiana
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Em ipkg
brand uses the
.Xr brands 7
framework to provide an environment for running a full copy of OpenIndiana,
with system software packages linked to those installed in the global zone.
By default, a package update in the global zone also updates core system
packages in linked
.Em ipkg
zones to keep them synchronised with the global zone.
Other packages can differ between the global zone and an
.Em ipkg
zone, subject to package dependencies.
.Pp
The
.Em nlipkg
brand uses the same environment without linking its package image to the
global zone.
Software in an
.Em nlipkg
zone is managed and updated independently.
Administrators must keep its core packages compatible with the global zone.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Use
.Xr zonecfg 8
to configure the zone and its network interfaces.
Configure persistent IP addresses and DNS resolver information inside the zone.
An example
.Em ipkg
zone using an existing VNIC called
.Sy vnic0
is shown below:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
create -t ipkg
set zonepath=/zones/testzone
set autoboot=true
set ip-type=exclusive
add net
    set physical=vnic0
end
.Ed
.Pp
To create an independently managed zone, use
.Sy create -t nlipkg
instead.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
.Em ipkg
zone boot environments are linked to the global zone boot environment under
which they were created.
This means that rolling back the global zone to a previous boot environment
will also roll back the zone.
For this reason, zone data which should be shared across boot environments
should be allocated to a dedicated dataset.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brands 7 ,
.Xr privileges 7 ,
.Xr resource_controls 7 ,
.Xr zones 7 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zoneadm 8 ,
.Xr zonecfg 8
